requirements.requirement:
Declare the handler with this exact signature and decorator:

@router.post("/links/{link_id}/tags", response_model=LinkWithTags, status_code=200)
def attach_tags(
    link_id: int,
    payload: TagAttach,
    db: Session = Depends(get_db),
) -> LinkWithTags:

The status code is 200, not 201. All three criteria this task implements specify 200 for the
success paths, and criterion 2 specifies 200 for a repeat post as well. The path has no /api
prefix; it is exactly `/links/{link_id}/tags`.

exports.interface:
# in app/api/links.py from fastapi import Depends from sqlalchemy.orm import Session from app.db import get_db from app.schemas.tag import LinkWithTags, TagAttach
@router.post("/links/{link_id}/tags", response_model=LinkWithTags, status_code=200) def attach_tags( link_id: int, payload: TagAttach, db: Session = Depends(get_db), ) -> LinkWithTags: """Attach tags to an existing link and return the link with every attached tag.
Tag names are matched case-sensitively. Attaching a tag already attached is a no-op that still returns 200. Raises HTTPException(404) when link_id does not exist, without creating any Tag or LinkTag row. """
